UPDATE companies SET description='Imtron Electronics was founded in 1988 and is headquartered in Eden Prairie, Minnesota.

Operating as a stocking distributor, Imtron maintains inventory from a roster of supplier partners that includes LEMO connectors, Magtech LED drivers, TXC crystals, Henkel thermal management products, and Mornsun power supplies. The product range spans connectors, crystals, thermal management solutions, and power supplies, supported by a consultative sales approach and global logistics.

The company serves manufacturers in the automotive, aviation, medical, and military sectors. Its components are specified in applications where field failure is not an option, such as defense systems, medical devices, avionics, and increasingly electrified vehicles.

Imtron differentiates itself through a consultative model aimed at identifying cost-effective solutions for high-reliability requirements. The company cites its ISO 9001:2015 certification and a team with decades of component-sourcing experience as foundations for supporting critical applications.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Electronic component distribution", "Consultative component selection", "Stocking and inventory management", "Global logistics", "Supplier partnership management"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Aviation", "Medical", "Military/Defense"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Consultative component selection for high-reliability applications", "Stocking distributor with inventory from LEMO, Magtech, TXC, Henkel, Mornsun", "ISO 9001:2015 certified quality management", "Decades of electronic component sourcing experience", "Global shipping to manufacturers in the U.S. and worldwide"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1988 -> db, /about", "Headquarters: Eden Prairie, Minnesota -> db, /about", "ISO 9001:2015 certified -> /, /about", "Stocking distributor of electronic components -> /about", "Supplier partners: LEMO, Magtech, TXC, Henkel, Mornsun -> /about", "Industries served: automotive, aviation, medical, military -> /", "Consultative approach for high-reliability applications -> /about", "Team includes Jeff Spaeth (President), Joe Schons, Julie Krull, Mike Dudkiewicz -> /about", "LinkedIn URL -> db"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Imtron Electronics is a stocking distributor of high-quality electronic components.", "founded_year": "1988", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": ["https://www.linkedin.com/company/imtron-electronics/"], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='imtron-electronics' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='In La Apparel operates as a vertically integrated apparel manufacturer based in Los Angeles and Orange County, California. The company, which does business as Apparel Branders Inc., specializes in private-label cut-and-sew production and full-package garment manufacturing. While a founding year is not publicly disclosed, the business emphasizes its mission to revitalize domestic clothing production through sweatshop-free, made-in-the-USA operations.

The company runs two manufacturing facilities in the Los Angeles area, including a knitting mill in the fashion district that produces fabrics such as cotton, synthetic blends, viscose/modal, polyester, melanges, organic, and slub yarns. In-house capabilities span pattern making, grading, marking, cutting, sewing, printing, embroidery, sublimation, heat transfer, deboss/emboss, cotton burnout, and reflective printing, along with fabric and garment dyeing. They handle orders from low-minimum sample runs to full-scale production, serving independent designers and established brands with a staff of around five employees.

In La Apparel serves the fashion industry, corporate and uniform programs, promotional products, and the entertainment sector. Clients include private-label apparel brands, corporate buyers seeking custom uniforms or promotional wear, and production studios in Los Angeles that need custom costumes for motion pictures, commercials, and television. The company also works directly with design teams to develop tailored production solutions.

The company positions itself on three pillars: customer service, creativity, and efficiency. It highlights its vertical integration—from fabric knitting through finishing—as a differentiator that shortens lead times and allows orders of any quantity. A stated commitment to sweatshop-free, domestic production and an "Organic Zone" for 100% organic apparel are cited as reasons clients choose them. Testimonials from brand managers and executives underscore on-time delivery and quality consistency.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Private label apparel manufacturing", "Cut and sew", "Knitting", "Fabric dyeing", "Garment dyeing", "Pattern making", "Grading", "Marking", "Cutting", "Sewing", "Printing", "Embroidery", "Sublimation", "Heat transfer", "Deboss/emboss", "Cotton burnout", "Reflective printing", "Packaging", "Fulfillment", "Design consulting", "Sample development", "Pre-production sampling", "Fabric development", "Digital media services"], "industries": ["Fashion", "Corporate uniforms", "Promotional products", "Entertainment (motion pictures, commercials, television)"], "materials": ["Cotton", "Synthetic blends", "Viscose/modal", "Polyester", "Melanges", "Organic cotton", "Slub yarns", "French Terry", "Mesh", "Modal spandex", "Tencel", "Bamboo", "Hacci", "Sweater fabric", "Micro modal"], "equipment": ["Garber System", "Knitting mill"], "volume": "Small batch to large scale production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Vertically integrated from knitting to finishing", "Low minimum order quantities", "Sweatshop-free, made-in-USA production", "Organic fabric capabilities", "In-house design and digital media services"], "facts_used": ["Location: Los Angeles & Orange County, California -> /about", "Vertically integrated, full-package apparel and cut-and-sew manufacturer -> /about", "Two factories, knitting mill in fashion district -> /", "In-house capabilities: pattern making, grading, marking, cutting, sewing, printing, embroidery, sublimation, heat transfer, deboss/emboss, cotton burnout, reflective printing, fabric/garment dyeing -> /about", "Low MOQ, volume production, small batch to large scale -> /about, /", "Staff of around five employees -> db", "Industries served: fashion, corporate, uniform, promotional, entertainment (motion pictures, commercials, television) -> /about, /", "Sweatshop-free, made-in-USA, organic zone -> /, /about", "Customer service, creativity, efficiency as differentiators -> /about", "Garber System mentioned -> /", "Materials: cotton, synthetic, viscose/modal, poly, melanges, organic, slub, French Terry, mesh, modal spandex, Tencel, bamboo, hacci, sweater fabric, micro modal -> /, /about", "Digital media services: graphic design, lookbook, e-commerce, photo shoots, branding, social media advertising -> /about"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "In La Apparel is a vertically integrated full package apparel and cut and sew manufacturers based in Los Angeles & Orange county, California United USA.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "5", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='in-la-apparel' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Index Packaging, Inc. operates from Milton, New Hampshire, where it has been based since 1981.

The firm designs and manufactures custom protective packaging for fragile or high‑value items, working across three material families — foam (polyurethane and polyethylene), wood (crates, pallets, and kiln‑dried lumber compliant with ISPM‑15), and corrugated fiberboard. Services extend to vendor‑managed inventory, just‑in‑time warehousing, and a dedicated trucking fleet for New England deliveries plus nationwide LTL, FedEx, and UPS shipping.

Customers span industrial equipment manufacturers, military and defense programs, medical, pharmaceutical, and laboratory sectors, and food and agriculture businesses. The company also produces retail‑focused lines such as foam‑filled apple gift shippers for specialty grocery and subscription boxes.

An in‑house recycling program diverts foam, corrugated, and wood scrap into secondary markets.', certifications=ARRAY['ISPM-15']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom packaging design and engineering", "Foam fabrication (polyurethane and polyethylene)", "Wood crate and pallet manufacturing", "Corrugated box manufacturing", "Kiln-drying to ISPM-15 standards", "Vendor-managed inventory (VMI)", "Warehousing and just-in-time delivery", "Trucking and logistics (own fleet + common carriers)", "Design, engineering & prototyping services", "DIY prototyping foam inserts", "Material sampling (FOB New Hampshire)", "In-house recycling of foam, corrugated, and wood scrap"], "industries": ["Industrial equipment manufacturing", "Military and defense", "Medical, pharmaceutical, and laboratory", "Food and agriculture"], "materials": ["Polyurethane foam", "Polyethylene foam", "Corrugated fiberboard", "Hardwood", "Softwood", "Wood (crates, pallets, lumber)"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house design & engineering at no cost to qualified buyers", "Nationwide shipping via LTL, FedEx, and UPS plus own New England fleet", "50+ years of experience in protective packaging", "Vendor-managed inventory and just-in-time warehousing services"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1968 by Bill and Connie Lander in New York basement -> /about-us", "Headquarters moved to Milton, NH in 1981 -> /about-us", "Family-owned, closely held corporation; second generation leadership (Bruce Lander) -> /about-us", "Board includes Bruce Lander (Chairman), Connie Lander, Debora Lussier -> /about-us", "Four NH facilities (Milton, Dover, Merrimack, Somersworth) totaling ~290,000 sq ft -> /about-us", "200+ employees -> /about-us", "Design and manufacturing of custom packaging for fragile/high-value items -> /about-us", "Materials: foam (polyurethane, polyethylene), wood, corrugated fiberboard -> /about-us", "Kiln-drying to ISPM-15 standards for export compliance -> /", "Industries served: industrial equipment, military, medical/pharmaceutical/labs, food/agriculture -> /about-us", "In-house design & engineering at no cost to qualified buyers -> /about-us, /services", "Vendor-managed inventory services -> /services", "Warehousing and just-in-time delivery -> /services", "Trucking & logistics with own fleet for New England, nationwide via LTL/FedEx/UPS -> /about-us, /services", "DIY prototyping foam inserts -> /services", "Material samples shipped FOB New Hampshire -> /services", "In-house recycling program for foam, corrugated, wood scrap -> /about-us", "Acquisitions: Timbertech (2002), Kerrigan Paper & Case Technology (2019), Plastifoam (2021), Aegis Container (2024), Avilite Corporation (2025) -> /about-us", "Apple gift pack boxes manufactured for retail/shipping -> /", "Website: indexpackaging.com -> db", "Location: Milton, New Hampshire -> db"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our specialty is design and manufacturing of custom packaging for fragile or high-value items.", "founded_year": "1968", "employee_count": "200+", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ISPM-15"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='index-packaging-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Industrial Fairway Supply, operating as IFS Packaging, is based in Fargo, North Dakota. The company has served the Midwest for over 40 years as a distributor of industrial packaging supplies and equipment.

The company distributes a broad line of packaging materials and equipment, including seals, pallets, rolled corrugate, strapping carts, steel and poly strapping, stretch wrap, foam bundles, corner and edge protectors, lumber wrap, industrial markers, composite staples, tools, and tape. Beyond product supply, IFS Packaging offers customized packaging solutions, providing personalized consultations to identify operational pain points and develop tailored strategies that improve efficiency, reduce waste, and optimize packaging budgets.

Industrial Fairway Supply serves customers throughout the United States, Canada, and internationally, building longstanding partnerships with businesses that require reliable packaging supplies and expertise.

The company emphasizes same-day shipping on stocked items, deep product knowledge, and problem-solving through innovative packaging ideas. Its consultative approach leverages the latest packaging technologies, including eco-friendly options, to help clients streamline processes and reduce costs. The True North Companies’ operating philosophy of servant leadership and empowering team members underpins a culture focused on preserving customer legacies and maintaining long-term relationships.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Industrial packaging supply distribution", "Custom packaging solution design", "Packaging consultation and assessment", "Same-day order fulfillment", "Packaging equipment sales"], "industries": [], "materials": ["Corrugated cardboard", "Steel strapping", "Poly strapping", "Stretch wrap", "Foam", "Lumber wrap", "Composite staples", "Industrial markers", "Tape"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "Same-day shipping on stocked items", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Same-day shipping on stocked packaging supplies", "Personalized one-on-one packaging consultations", "Custom packaging solutions tailored to specific operational challenges", "Access to latest packaging technologies and eco-friendly options", "Servant-leadership culture focused on long-term customer partnerships"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Fargo, North Dakota -> db", "Over 40 years in business as a distributor of industrial packaging supplies and equipment -> db", "Same-day shipping, product quality, product knowledge, problem-solving, innovative packaging ideas -> db", "Partnerships throughout US, Canada, and beyond -> db", "Product list: Seals, Pallets, Rolled Corrugate, Strapping Cart, Steel and Poly Strapping, Colored Stretch Wrap, Stretch Wrap, Foam Bundles, Corner and Edge Protectors, Lumber Wrap and Sewn Covers, Industrial Markers, Composite Staples, Tools, Tape -> /", "Custom packaging solutions, personalized one-on-one consultations -> /about", "Leveraging latest packaging technologies, eco-friendly options -> /about", "True North Companies operating philosophy: servant leadership, small family business feeling, long-term cultural stability, empowering team members, preserving legacies -> /about"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Industrial Fairway Supply has set the standard as the Midwest\u2019s leading distributor of industrial packaging supplies and equipment.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='industrial-fairway-supply' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Industrial Food Ingredients Co. is headquartered in Hunt Valley, Maryland, and has been family-owned since its founding in 1989. The company operates from a Hunt Valley office with a mailing address in Westminster, and serves customers across the Mid-Atlantic region including Delaware, Maryland, New Jersey, New York, Pennsylvania, Virginia, Washington, D.C., and West Virginia.

The firm acts as an ingredient supplier, providing a broad range of food ingredients for finished products. Its portfolio includes nuts, fruits, vegetables, and specialty items such as chocolate coatings, fillings, coatings, and grinds. The company emphasizes end-to-end service, offering product sampling for new product development, contract management with regular updates, market price monitoring, and document fulfillment.

Its customer base spans confectionery, ice cream, natural foods, and broader food manufacturing sectors. The company maintains memberships with the American Association of Candy Technologists, the North East Ice Cream Association, the Pennsylvania Manufacturing Confectioners Association, the Institute of Food Technologists, and the Research Chefs Association, reflecting its focus on these industries.

Founded on a philosophy that communication is the key ingredient to success, Industrial Food Ingredients Co. differentiates itself through personalized service, prompt responsiveness, and proactive market intelligence. The leadership team, including President Scott Hetherington and Vice President of Sales Sharon Black, underscores a commitment to money-saving proposals, crop updates, and new ingredient information for clients.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Ingredient sourcing and supply", "Product sampling for development", "Contract management", "Market price monitoring", "Technical product knowledge support", "New ingredient information", "Crop updates", "Money-saving proposals", "Document fulfillment"], "industries": ["Confectionery", "Ice Cream", "Natural Foods", "Food Manufacturing", "Research & Development"], "materials": ["Nuts", "Fruits", "Vegetables", "Chocolate Coatings", "Fillings", "Grinds"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["End-to-end order service", "Contract management with regular updates", "Market condition monitoring and competitive pricing", "Product sample requests for development", "Document fulfillment support"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1989, family-owned, Hunt Valley MD -> db and /", "Ingredient supplier for finished products -> /", "Ingredients: nuts, fruits, vegetables, chocolate coatings, fillings, coatings, grinds -> /", "Service area: DE, MD, NJ, NY, PA, VA, DC, WV -> /", "Key personnel: Scott Hetherington (President), Sharon Black (VP Sales), Penny Kirdy (Office Manager), Theresa Mauldin (Customer Service) -> /", "Associations: American Association of Candy Technologists, F.I.N.D. Group, Institute of Food Technologists, Natural Products Food Expo, North East Ice Cream Association, Pennsylvania Manufacturing Confectioners Association, Research Chefs Association -> /", "Mission statement services: end-to-end order service, contract management, market monitoring, product knowledge, samples, document fulfillment, crop updates, money-saving proposals -> /"], "company_type": "Distributor / reseller", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "Industrial Food Ingredients Co. based in Hunt Valley, Maryland, is an ingredient supplier providing sales of all types of ingredients for finished products.", "founded_year": "1989", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": ["Family-owned"]}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='industrial-food-ingredients-co' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Industrial Packaging Corporation was founded in 1988 in Tomahawk, Wisconsin. The company now operates from its headquarters in Wilton, Iowa, with additional facilities in Arcadia, Wisconsin; Fort Payne, Alabama; and Tomahawk, Wisconsin.

The company manufactures a range of recyclable packaging products including corrugated angle pads, honeycomb pads and packaging, shaft packs, and wine bottle packs. Its capabilities include corrugated pad manufacturing, honeycomb fabrication, and non-scuff coating, supported by a custom design service called Vision Design. Production occurs across four U.S. facilities.

Industrial Packaging Corporation serves the packaging industry and supplies components for metal bathroom partitions, wine bottling, and industrial shipping. Its structural honeycomb is used inside metal bathroom partitions, while honeycomb pads and risers are employed to block and brace products in transit. The company also provides specialized packs for wine bottles and shafts.

The company emphasizes that all its packaging is recyclable, with more than half of the paper purchased made from 100 percent recycled content. All products have been manufactured in the United States since the company''s inception in 1988.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Corrugated angle pad manufacturing", "Honeycomb pad and packaging fabrication", "Non-scuff coating application", "Custom packaging design (Vision Design)", "Shaft pack manufacturing", "Wine bottle pack manufacturing", "Structural honeycomb fabrication for bathroom partitions", "Block and brace packaging solutions"], "industries": ["Packaging", "Bathroom partitions", "Wine and beverage", "Industrial shipping and logistics"], "materials": ["Paper", "Recycled paper fibers", "100% recycled content paper", "Corrugated cardboard", "Structural honeycomb"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["All packaging is recyclable", "Over half of paper sourced from 100% recycled content", "Made in the USA since 1988", "Custom packaging design through Vision Design service", "Four U.S. manufacturing locations"], "facts_used": ["Founded in 1988 in Tomahawk, Wisconsin -> page:/", "Headquarters in Wilton, Iowa -> db, page:/", "Facilities in Tomahawk WI, Arcadia WI, Fort Payne AL, Wilton IA -> page:/", "Products: Corrugated Angle Pads, Honeycomb Pads & Packaging, Shaft Pack, Wine Bottle Pack -> page:/", "Capability: Angle Frame Non-Scuff Coating Corrugated Pads -> db", "All packaging recyclable, made with recycled fibers, >50% paper from 100% recycled content -> db, page:/", "Made in USA since 1988 -> page:/", "Vision Design custom design service -> page:/", "Structural honeycomb used in metal bathroom partitions -> page:/", "Honeycomb pads/risers for blocking and bracing in transit -> page:/", "Sales managers: Ron Donais, Dan Horton, Bill Bryan -> page:/"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "All packaging manufactured by Industrial Packaging Corporation is recyclable.", "founded_year": "1988", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='industrial-packaging-corporation' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Infant Ear Molding of New Hampshire, LLC operates from Fremont, New Hampshire. The clinic was founded by Dr. Emily Hurst, who holds a Doctor of Science degree from Massachusetts College of Pharmacy and Health Sciences and a background in pediatric plastic surgery. Recognizing limited access to noninvasive ear correction for infants, she established the first clinic in the state dedicated solely to professional ear molding services.

The company provides a noninvasive, nonmedical ear molding service that uses malleable splints to reshape infant ear cartilage while it remains pliable, typically before three months of age. The process is described as comfortable and straightforward, usually lasting about six weeks.

The service targets families with infants who have prominent or misshapen ears, aiming to prevent psychosocial stress, teasing, and future surgical otoplasty. Customers are primarily parents seeking early intervention for congenital auricular deformities, with the clinic referencing pediatric plastic surgery and infant care as relevant fields.

The clinic emphasizes its status as New Hampshire''s first dedicated infant ear molding provider and cites published studies supporting the safety, efficacy, and high parent satisfaction of ear molding therapy. The approach is positioned as an evidence-based alternative that avoids the complications of surgical correction.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Infant ear molding", "Ear splint application", "Noninvasive ear correction", "Congenital auricular deformity treatment"], "industries": ["Pediatric plastic surgery", "Infant care", "Healthcare services"], "materials": ["Medical-grade malleable splints"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["First clinic in New Hampshire solely dedicated to infant ear molding", "Noninvasive, nonmedical service using malleable splints", "Leverages cartilage malleability window before three months of age", "Avoids need for surgical otoplasty and associated complications", "Supported by peer-reviewed evidence of safety and high parent satisfaction"], "facts_used": ["Company name and service description -> /", "Location: Fremont, New Hampshire 03044 -> /", "Founder: Dr. Emily Hurst with education background -> /", "Clinic is first dedicated infant ear molding clinic in New Hampshire -> /", "Process: malleable splint, cartilage hardens around 3 months, takes 6 weeks -> /", "Target customers: families/parents seeking to avoid surgery -> /", "Reference to study (Vu et al. 2020) on safety and satisfaction -> /", "Contact info: phone and email -> /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "offers professional ear molding service which can help correct the shape of your child''s ears. This noninvasive, nonmedical service involves using a malleable splint to hold the ear cartilage in the corrected shape", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='infant-ear-molding-of-new-hampshire-llc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Infineon Technologies Americas operates a U.S. design center in Austin, Texas, established in 1999 as part of the global Infineon Technologies group. The subsidiary focuses on power and security semiconductors for automotive and industrial markets.

The company designs, develops, manufactures, and markets a broad portfolio including power management ICs, microcontrollers, security ICs, Silicon Carbide MOSFET modules, IGBT modules, automotive MOSFETs, current sensors, stepper and servo motor drivers, 3D magnetic sensors, and protection ICs. Globally, Infineon reports 58,000 employees across 71 R&D sites and 15 manufacturing locations, with annual revenue of approximately €15 billion; the Americas division employs between 3,000 and 9,999 people.

Its products serve automotive, industrial, IoT, AI and communication, security, and consumer electronics sectors. Concrete applications include electric vehicle powertrains, renewable energy infrastructure, industrial motor control, and secure IoT devices.

Infineon positions itself as a world leader in semiconductor solutions, emphasizing a developer ecosystem with 125,000+ solutions, 160,000+ engineers, and 1,700+ code repositories, alongside cloud and engineering support services that accelerate time-to-market. The company states its mission is to make life easier, safer, and greener through energy-efficient, secure mobility and smart IoT.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Semiconductor design and development", "Semiconductor manufacturing (front-end and back-end)", "Cloud-based development platforms", "Engineering and consulting services", "Design-in support", "Software and tool provision for evaluation", "Developer community and technical support", "Power semiconductor fabrication (SiC, IGBT, MOSFET)", "Microcontroller and security IC development", "Sensor development (current, 3D magnetic)"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Industrial", "IoT", "AI & Communication", "Security", "Consumer Electronics"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Global footprint: 58,000+ employees, 71 R&D sites, 15 manufacturing locations", "Developer community: 125,000+ solutions, 160,000+ engineers, 1,700+ code repositories", "Cloud and engineering support services for integrated development ecosystem", "Design-in support for application-specific requirements", "Broad semiconductor portfolio spanning power, security, sensing, and microcontrollers"], "facts_used": ["Headquarters in Austin, Texas -> db", "Founded 1999 -> db", "Employee count 3000-9999 -> db", "Designs, develops, manufactures, markets semiconductors -> /", "58K+ employees worldwide, 71 R&D sites, 15 manufacturing locations, ~\u20ac15Bn revenue -> /", "Products: Power Semiconductors, Microcontrollers, Security ICs, SiC MOSFET modules, IGBT modules, Automotive MOSFETs, Current sensors, Stepper/servo drivers, 3D sensors, Protection ICs, CoolSET -> /", "Industries: Automotive, Industrial, IoT, AI & Communication, Security, Consumer -> /, db", "Developer community: 125K+ solutions, 160K+ engineers, 1700+ code repositories -> /", "Cloud and engineering support services -> /services", "Design-in support -> /services", "Mission: make life easier, safer, greener -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Infineon designs, develops, manufactures, and markets a broad range of solutions.", "founded_year": "1999", "employee_count": "3000-9999", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='infineon-technologies-americas' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Infinity Molding & Assembly, Inc. has operated from Mt. Vernon, Indiana since 1982.

The company specializes in custom plastic injection molding for difficult geometries and engineering-grade thermoplastics, including high-heat resins that require hot-oil mold temperature control. Its equipment roster spans 55- to 500-ton presses, supported by robotics from Yushin, Staubli, Star Automation, Rethink Robotics and Universal Robots. A separate 11,000-square-foot ISO Class 8 cleanroom provides dedicated medical molding and white-room assembly, while electronic vision systems handle in-line inspection.

The medical cleanroom is noted as the only one of its kind within a 300-mile radius, and the automotive line carries IATF 16949 certification.

Leadership emphasizes domestic production — President and CEO Scott Titzer and Executive Vice President and CFO Sondra Ash highlight the cleanroom’s regional uniqueness and the workforce’s ability to deliver high-precision parts quickly.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001','ISO 13485','ISO 14001','IATF 16949']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom plastic injection molding", "Cleanroom molding (ISO Class 8)", "White room assembly", "Automotive parts molding", "Medical device molding", "Engineering-grade thermoplastic processing", "High-heat resin processing", "Hot-oil mold temperature control", "Robotics automation", "Electronic vision inspection", "Secondary assembly operations"], "industries": ["Medical devices", "Automotive", "Consumer goods", "Industrial"], "materials": ["Engineering-grade thermoplastics", "High-heat resins"], "equipment": ["Injection molding machines (55-500 tons)", "Yushin robots", "Staubli robots", "Star Automation equipment", "Rethink Robotics", "Universal Robots", "Electronic vision inspection systems"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Only ISO Class 8 medical cleanroom within 300 miles", "Robotics integration with Yushin, Staubli, Star Automation, Rethink Robotics, Universal Robots", "Electronic vision inspection for quality assurance", "Injection molding capacity from 55 to 500 tons", "Certified to ISO 9001, ISO 13485, ISO 14001, IATF 16949"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1982 -> db", "Headquarters Mt Vernon, Indiana -> db", "Certifications ISO 13485, IATF 16949, ISO 14001, ISO 9001 -> db", "Custom plastic injection molder, difficult geometries, engineering grade thermoplastics, high heat resins, hot oil systems -> /", "Two facilities: Automotive/Industrial and Medical/Healthcare on same property -> /", "Machine sizes 55 to 500 tons -> /", "Separate 11,000 sq ft ISO Class 8 cleanroom manufacturing and white room assembly -> /", "Robotics: Yushin, Staubli, Star Automation, Rethink Robotics, Universal Robots ->