UPDATE companies SET description='Interstate Telecommunications Cooperative (ITC) operates from its headquarters in Brookings, South Dakota. The cooperative provides telecommunications services across its service territory, though the founding year and original founders are not publicly disclosed in the available materials.

ITC delivers a suite of communications services for both residential and business customers. Residential offerings include fiber-based internet, traditional phone service, and streaming television. For businesses, the cooperative provides integrated voice and data solutions, managed IT services, and a managed Wi-Fi platform branded as Blast Wi-Fi. A newer feature, SmartTown®, extends managed Wi-Fi access beyond the home. The company also handles the Federal Universal Service Charge adjustments as required by regulation.

The customer base spans households and organizations of any size, from small businesses to large corporations. ITC participates in the Medicaid/Medical Assistance program, offering discounted internet service to qualifying subscribers. Business customers receive tailored voice and data packages, while residential users can choose from various internet speed tiers and streaming TV options.

The cooperative emphasizes local management of Wi-Fi networks through Blast Wi-Fi, giving subscribers the choice of provider-managed or self-managed wireless. Paperless billing is incentivized with bill credits and prize drawings. These service differentiators reflect ITC’s focus on customer control and community-oriented service delivery.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Fiber internet service", "Voice over IP (VoIP) phone service", "Streaming television", "Managed Wi-Fi (Blast Wi-Fi)", "SmartTown Wi-Fi extension", "Managed IT services", "Business voice and data solutions", "Federal Universal Service Charge administration"], "industries": ["Residential telecommunications", "Business telecommunications", "Healthcare (Medicaid/Medical Assistance)"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Fiber-based internet service to residential and business customers", "Blast Wi-Fi managed wireless platform with provider- or self-managed options", "SmartTown\u00ae extending managed Wi-Fi access beyond the home", "Integrated voice and data solutions for businesses of any size", "Paperless billing with instant bill credit and prize incentives"], "facts_used": ["Company name and headquarters: db", "Services and offerings: /", "Medicaid/Medical Assistance program: /", "Blast Wi-Fi and SmartTown features: /", "Paperless billing rewards: /", "Federal Universal Service Charge updates: /"], "company_type": "Installer / service company", "makes_products": "no", "type_evidence": "ITC offers a full-range of integrated voice and data solutions.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='interstate-telecommunications-cooperative' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='Interstate Wire Co Inc was established in 1977 and is headquartered in Rockwall, Texas. The company operates as a distributor of electronic and electrical wire, cable, and wire management products, leveraging partnerships with manufacturers such as Belden, General Cable, Harbour Industries, and Thomas & Betts.

The company''s core offerings include hook-up wire, multi-conductor cable, coaxial cables, portable cordage, flat cable, molded cable assemblies, and related wire management products. Beyond distribution, Interstate Wire provides value-added wire preparation services such as respooling, shrink-wrapping, twisting, and striping, as well as pre-production preparation including light assembly and custom kitting to streamline customer workflows.

Interstate Wire serves a range of industries including automotive and transportation OEMs, power distribution (switchgear, control panels), building systems (electrical, HVAC, security, fire protection), medical devices, military and aerospace, marine, and mining and construction. Its customers include OEMs and sub-assemblers requiring high-quality wire and cable for demanding applications.

