UPDATE companies SET description='J G Plastics Group LLC operates from Costa Mesa, California, where it was founded in 1975.

The facility runs as a complete plastic injection molding operation covering both thermoplastic and thermoset materials. Capabilities include precision molding, close-tolerance work, in-mold decoration, insert molding, overmolding, and medical mesh overmolding. A 2,000-square-foot Class 10,000 (ISO 7) cleanroom supports medical-grade molding and assembly, while an in-house mold making department uses CAD/CAM software to build complex tooling. Secondary services span assembly, decoration, painting, shielding, and packaging.

The company serves medical, aerospace, defense/military/tactical, electronic/connector, and consumer markets. Customers include manufacturers requiring components that meet FAA and MIL-SPEC regulations, as well as medical device makers needing cleanroom assembly and packaging.

J G Plastics emphasizes its ability to tackle demanding, close-tolerance parts through scientific molding principles and decades of tooling experience. It highlights ITAR registration, adherence to Good Manufacturing Practices, and a location adjacent to John Wayne Airport that facilitates shipping across the United States, Canada, Mexico, Europe, and Asia.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','AS9100D','ISO 13485:2016','ITAR registered']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Plastic injection molding (thermoplastic and thermoset)", "Mold making", "Assembly and secondary operations", "Medical device assembly", "Close tolerance molding", "In-mold decoration", "Insert molding", "Overmolding", "Medical mesh overmolding", "Class 10,000 cleanroom molding", "Class 10,000 cleanroom assembly", "Thermoset molding"], "industries": ["Medical", "Aerospace", "Defense / Military / Tactical", "Electronic / Connector", "Consumer"], "materials": ["TPE/TPU/TPV elastomers", "Conductive & shielding plastics", "High strength plastics", "Medical grade plastics", "PPS and LCP plastics", "Elvax (EVA) copolymer resins"], "equipment": ["Horizontal and vertical injection molding machines", "CAD/CAM software"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["In-house mold making with CAD/CAM tooling design", "Class 10,000 (ISO 7) cleanroom for medical molding and assembly", "Scientific molding principles for close-tolerance parts", "ITAR registered and compliant with FAA/MIL-SPEC requirements", "Good Manufacturing Practices (GMP) for medical devices"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1975 -> db", "Headquarters Costa Mesa, California -> db", "Certifications ISO 9001:2015, AS9100D, ISO 13485:2016, ITAR -> db and /", "Capabilities: plastic injection molding, mold making, assembly, cleanroom molding, thermoset molding -> /capabilities", "Industries served: Medical, Aerospace, Defense/Military/Tactical, Electronic/Connector, Consumer -> /", "Materials: TPE/TPU/TPV, conductive plastics, high