UPDATE companies SET description='J Miller Handcrafted Furniture operates from a converted post office building in Chicago, Illinois. A former classical musician, Miller began his career crafting furniture that has since been exhibited in galleries nationwide.

The shop produces handcrafted furniture using a range of woodworking equipment, including two table saws, two jointer/planers, two bandsaws, a drill press, stroke and edge sanders, two lathes, and seven workbenches. The facility also maintains an extensive collection of hand and power tools for joinery and detail work. No headcount or annual volume figures are disclosed.

Miller’s furniture has been shown in galleries and shows across the country and has won numerous awards. His pieces are held in the Decorative Arts Collection of the Chicago History Museum.

The company distinguishes itself through Miller’s dual role as a practicing craftsman and an educator; his published books and instructional videos on chairmaking, beds, and children’s furniture reflect a commitment to advancing woodworking technique. This expertise informs the design and construction of each piece.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom furniture design", "Handcrafted furniture production", "Wood joinery", "Wood turning", "Sanding and finishing", "Furniture prototyping"], "industries": ["Furniture manufacturing", "Woodworking", "Decorative arts", "Galleries", "Museums"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["2 tablesaws", "jointer", "2 jointer/planers", "2 bandsaws", "drill press", "stroke sander", "edge sander", "joinery tools", "2 lathes", "7 workbenches", "hand and hand power tools"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Award-winning furniture featured in the Chicago History Museum''s Decorative Arts Collection", "Shop equipped with professional-grade woodworking machinery including dual table saws, jointer/planers, and lathes", "Furniture exhibited in galleries and shows nationwide"], "facts_used": ["Located in Chicago, Illinois -> db", "Founded by Jeff Miller, furniture designer, craftsman, teacher, author -> /about", "Shop in converted post office building with listed equipment -> db", "Furniture shown in galleries nationwide, won awards, in Chicago History Museum collection -> /about", "Jeff Miller authored multiple woodworking books -> /about"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Our shop is set up in an old post office building, and is spacious and well equipped, with 2 tablesaws, a jointer, 2 jointer/planers, 2 bandsaws, drill press, stroke sander, edge sander, joinery tools, 2 lathes, 7 workbenches, and numerous top quality hand and hand power tools.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='j-miller-handcrafted-furniture' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='J. Alexander Fine Woodworking operates from Nampa, Idaho, in the Treasure Valley. The business traces its roots to 1991 when Jared Patchin’s father purchased Shutter Crafts, a local wood-shutter manufacturer. Patchin spent his youth in the shop turning scrap wood into rickety tables, chairs, desks, and wooden swords. After studying civil engineering and later production management at Boise State University, he applied those disciplines to woodworking and has led J. Alexander for 17 years.

The shop produces residential cabinetry and high-end furniture, blending computerized CNC machining with traditional hand techniques. Every piece is first rendered in a 3D environment to verify specifications, then translated into digital drawings that drive exact cut-outs on the CNC equipment. The team also relies on seasoned hand craftsmanship for joinery and finishing, allowing both precision and custom detail.

The firm emphasizes continuous learning, adopting new software and building methods while retaining the hands-on approach that began with a handsaw and scrap lumber.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["3D rendering", "CNC machining", "Digital design", "Hand woodworking", "Custom furniture construction", "Cabinetry construction"], "industries": ["Residential cabinetry", "Fine furniture"], "materials": [], "equipment": ["CNC machine"], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["3D rendering for accurate specifications", "CNC machining paired with hand craftsmanship", "Digital design driving exact cut-outs", "Continuous innovation in building methods"], "facts_used": ["Jared Patchin started building furniture in 1991 when his father bought Shutter Crafts -> /", "Located in Nampa, Idaho (Treasure Valley) -> db", "Has been running J. Alexander for 17 years -> /", "Studied civil engineering then production management at Boise State University -> /", "Renders all products in a 3D environment ensuring accurate specifications -> /about-us", "Uses state-of-the-art designing software for precise measurements using digital drawings and exact cut-outs from computerized CNC machine and by hand -> /about-us", "Seasoned professionals that love what they''re doing, implement building methods that work best, always learning and innovating -> /about-us", "Makes residential cabinetry and fine furniture (end tables, chairs, desks, swords) -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "Jared Patchin started building furniture in 1991 when his father bought Shutter Crafts.", "founded_year": "", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='j-alexander-fine-woodworking' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='J.Q. Dickinson Salt-Works operates from Charleston, West Virginia. The business traces its roots to a family that produced salt in the region for more than 120 years, when the area was the nation''s salt producer with over 50 businesses and 100 wells. In 2013, siblings Nancy Bruns and Lewis Payne revived the family enterprise, reestablishing the J.Q. Dickinson name.

The company harvests natural sea salt from ancient ocean brine trapped beneath the Appalachian Mountains. Using traditional slow-sun-drying methods, they produce small-batch finishing salts, cooking salts, and flavored varieties such as ramp, applewood smoked, and bourbon-barrel aged. The operation also curates a line of artisanal pantry goods, home fragrances, and gift sets sourced from regional makers.

Products are sold directly to consumers through an online mercantile and offered wholesale to retailers and specialty food shops.

The revival was driven by a desire to preserve Appalachian salt-making heritage and showcase the mineral-rich character of the local brine. The founders emphasize small-batch craftsmanship and partnerships with artisans who share their commitment to authenticity.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Hand-harvesting", "Slow-sun-drying", "Small-batch blending", "Flavoring (ramp, applewood smoked, bourbon-barrel aged)", "Gift set curation", "Wholesale distribution"], "industries": ["Food & Beverage", "Specialty Food", "Retail", "Wholesale"], "materials": ["Appalachian ocean brine", "Sea salt", "Ramp", "Applewood smoke", "Bourbon barrel"], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Salt harvested from ancient Appalachian ocean brine", "Slow-sun-dried using traditional methods", "Small-batch production", "Flavored salts include ramp, applewood smoked, bourbon-barrel aged", "Partnerships with regional artisans for curated goods"], "facts_used": ["Company name: J.Q. Dickinson Salt-Works -> db", "Location: Charleston, West Virginia -> db", "Historical family production over 120 years, region leading producer -> db", "Revival in 2013 by Nancy Bruns and Lewis Payne -> db", "Harvest salt from ancient ocean brine under Appalachian Mountains -> /", "Slow-sun-dried, small-batch methods -> /", "Flavored salts: ramp, applewood smoked, bourbon-barrel aged -> /", "Curate artisanal goods from regional makers -> /", "Sell direct and wholesale -> /", "Contact for wholesale: phone and email -> /"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "As an artisan salt company, we rely on small-batch methods to retain the true essence of natural sea salt.", "founded_year": "2013", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='j-q-dickinson-salt-works' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='JAMM Fabrication & Design was founded in 2017 in North Little Rock, Arkansas, by co-owners Matt Goodhart and Allen Walker. Walker, who began welding in high school and later attended Nashville Auto Diesel College, identified a need for custom train car handrails and taught himself to fabricate them. Goodhart, introduced by a mutual friend, saw an opportunity to start a fabrication company and partnered with Walker to launch the business.

The team of 24 employees ships roughly 50,000 custom parts per month from their North Little Rock facility, with a second location opened in spring 2025 and a Texas site planned.

JAMM serves architecture and construction firms (structural components, railings), manufacturers and industrial clients (conveyor parts, assembled configurations), and individuals and businesses seeking custom specialty items such as sculptures, fixtures, and signage. Customers include Heating and Cooling Systems of Arkansas, which uses them for commercial projects.

The founders started the company to fill a gap in well-built custom handrails for train cars, and their mission emphasizes aligning experience, capabilities, and technology to build customers'' dreams while fostering a supportive environment for their team. They highlight free quotes, in-house certified welding, and a single-source approach from design through finishing.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Fiber optic laser cutting (flat and tube)", "CNC press brake forming", "5-axis CNC pipe bending", "Plate rolling", "Powder coating", "Welding (MIG, TIG, Stick)", "Sandblasting", "CNC machining (milling and turning)", "Custom & specialty fabrication (design, sculpture, signage)"], "industries": ["Architecture & Construction", "Manufacturing & Industrial", "Custom & Specialty Jobs"], "materials": ["Steel", "Aluminum", "Stainless Steel"], "equipment": ["Fiber optic laser (60.25\" x 120.25\" cutting area, 24 GA to 2\" thick)", "220 ton CNC press brake (up to 10 ft length)", "5-axis CNC pipe bender (up to 3-1/2\" OD)", "Plate roller (18 gauge to 3/8\" thickness, including stainless steel)", "Powder coat booth with 8x8x30 ft oven", "7 CNC lathes and CNC mills (largest mill 30\" x 60\", large lathe 14\" round bar up to 20 ft)"], "volume": "Prototype to high-volume production (approximately 50,000 parts per month)", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Free quotes on all projects", "In-house certified welding (MIG, TIG, Stick)", "Single-source fabrication: laser, forming, welding, powder coating under one roof", "50,000 custom parts shipped monthly", "7 CNC lathes and mills for prototype to high-volume production"], "facts_used": ["Founded 2017 -> /about", "Founders Matt Goodhart and Allen Walker -> /about", "24 employees -> /about", "50,000 custom parts per month -> /about", "North Little Rock, Arkansas headquarters -> db", "Fiber optic laser cutting 60.25x120.25\" -> /services", "220 ton CNC press brake -> /services", "5-axis CNC pi