UPDATE companies SET description='JEM Electronics, Inc. was founded in 1981 by John McDonald in Franklin, Massachusetts.

Today JEM operates from its headquarters in Franklin, MA, and a production facility in Tijuana, Mexico, providing build-to-print manufacturing from prototype through high-volume production. Core capabilities include custom cable assembly, complex wire harness assembly, and integrated box-build electromechanical assembly. Every assembly undergoes 100% in-house testing—continuity, pull, hipot, and VSWR—under documented procedures aligned with IPC/WHMA-A-620 workmanship standards. The company employs cross-trained assemblers and applies Lean Six Sigma methods to maintain process consistency.

JEM serves OEMs in regulated, high-reliability sectors including military and defense, medical, semiconductor, robotics, renewable energy, oil and gas, and networking. Its ITAR registration and CAGE code 3DTF7 support defense and government contract work, while ISO 9001:2015 and UL/CSA certifications cover commercial and industrial requirements.

The company differentiates itself by reviewing every drawing for manufacturability before quoting, delivering transparent timelines, and standing behind each assembly with full traceability documentation. McDonald’s original vision—to solve customer problems through modern technology and repeatable quality—remains the guiding principle behind JEM’s disciplined, documented process from drawing to delivery.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','IPC/WHMA-A-620','ITAR','IPC-A-620','IPC-J-STD-001','UL/CSA']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Custom cable assembly", "Wire harness assembly", "Electromechanical box-build assembly", "Build-to-print manufacturing", "Rapid prototyping", "Scalable production", "Continuity and resistance testing", "VSWR testing (S21/S22)", "Hipot testing", "Pull testing", "Design for manufacturability review", "Supply chain management", "Lean Six Sigma process improvement", "Cross-trained assembler program", "UL/CSA certified manufacturing", "ITAR-compliant production"], "industries": ["Military & Defense", "Medical", "Semiconductor", "Robotics", "Renewable Energy", "Oil & Gas", "Networking"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "Prototype to high-volume production", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["100% in-house testing (continuity, pull, hipot, VSWR) on every assembly", "ITAR registered with CAGE code 3DTF7 for defense and government work", "ISO 9001:2015 and IPC/WHMA-A-620 certified facilities in the US and Mexico", "Cross-trained assemblers and Lean Six Sigma process controls", "Manufacturability review on every drawing before quote"], "facts_used": ["Founded 1981 by John McDonald -> /about-us", "Headquarters in Franklin, MA; production facility in Tijuana, MX -> /about-us", "ISO 9001:2015, IPC/WHMA-A-620, ITAR, IPC-A-620, IPC-J-STD-001, UL/CSA certifications -> /quality", "CAGE code 3DTF7 -> /", "Capabilities: custom cable assembly, wire harness, electromechanical assembly -> /", "Industries served: Military & Defense, Medical, Semiconductor, Robotics, Renewable Energy, Oil & Gas, Networking -> /", "100% in-house testing (continuity, pull, hipot, VSWR) -> /quality", "Cross-trained assemblers, Lean Six Sigma -> /quality", "Build-to-print from prototype to high-volume production -> /", "ITAR registered for defense work -> /", "Founder John McDonald vision to modernize cable manufacturing -> /about-us"], "company_type": "Contract manufacturer / job shop", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "A US-based contract manufacturer since 1981.", "founded_year": "1981", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "3DTF7", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": ["ITAR registered"], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='jem-electronics-inc' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='JFD-PK Medical LLC is based in Center Valley, Pennsylvania. The company was founded by Dr. Jameel Durrani, a board‑certified pulmonologist and critical care physician with more than 20 years of clinical experience. Dr. Durrani established the business to translate his frontline expertise into innovative solutions for critically ill patients.

The company develops and manufactures a range of critical‑care devices, including chest drainage systems, vascular guidewire technologies, and long‑term pleural drainage catheters.

Its products are intended for clinicians and hospitals practicing critical care medicine, with a focus on bedside procedures such as thoracic drainage and vascular access. The company collaborates directly with physicians to refine device design for real‑world clinical use.

