 -> /", "AWS D17.2 spot-weld certified, Class C at 2,000 lbs -> /", "AWS D1.3 plug-weld certified -> /", "First Article Reports to AS9102 standards available -> /quality", "Industries served: Aerospace, Medical, Electronics -> /", "Processes: laser cutting, forming, CNC machining, welding, punching, hardware installation, assembly -> /about-us", "Finishing partnerships for plating, anodizing, painting, powder coating, silk-screening -> /about-us", "Quality measuring equipment: Fabrivision Part Inspection Scanner, Tesa Hite Gauge 700, 24\" Digital Dimension Inspection Table, 80\" Digital Calipers, 24\" Digital Calipers, 24\" Vernier Calipers, 12\" & 24\" Height Gauges, Pocket Surf Portable Roughness Gauge, Fowler Bower Holematic .250-.750 Diameter Gauge, Digital Force Gauge for Hardware Inspection, Calibrated Pin Gauges, Calibrated Surface Plate, SolidWorks First Article Software with AS9102 Reporting -> /quality", "48\" wide shear and laser cutting capabilities -> /", "Commitment to 98% internal/customer acceptance rate and 98% on-time delivery -> /quality"], "company_type": "Manufacturer", "makes_products": "yes", "type_evidence": "to be an outstanding precision sheet metal and machining manufacturer for the Aerospace, Medical and Electronics industries", "founded_year": "1986", "employee_count": "", "cage_code": "", "min_order": "", "export_compliance": [], "languages": [], "social_links": [], "ownership_tags": []}'::jsonb, updated_at=now() WHERE slug='jit-manufacturing' AND approved AND profile IS NULL;
UPDATE companies SET description='JJISCO, Inc. has been supporting customer requirements from its headquarters in Oconomowoc, Wisconsin since 1998. The company was formally organized in 2000 as a wholly owned subsidiary of a 40-year-old parent organization, taking its name from the founder''s initials combined with "Innovative Solutions Company."

The company manufactures custom engineered components from hard materials including silicon carbide, tungsten carbide, alumina, and zirconia ceramics. Its product range covers seals, bushings, shafts, nozzles, wear rings, thrust plates, valve components, frac plug buttons, large-diameter seal faces, semiconductor parts, burst discs, bearings, magnetic-drive components, and rotary steerable system components. JJISCO also provides material selection, design-for-manufacturability assistance, sub-contract assembly, supply-chain optimization, and inventory programs such as just-in-time and Kanban-supported warehousing. Its Wisconsin facility handles both high- and low-volume production.

Customers rely on the company for both standard and custom components, often involving collaborative development from concept through packaging.

