UPDATE companies SET description='JUNE Medical USA Inc is based in New Castle, Delaware, serving as the U.S. entity of JUNE Medical, a privately owned medical device group with offices in the United Kingdom, the United States, and Sweden. The company manages early-stage innovation, research and development, manufacturing, and global commercialization through its sister company Mosaic Surgical, which acts as the manufacturing arm. The name "JUNE" began as a secret code name before launch, chosen to represent spring, growth, and the future; no founding year or individual founders are disclosed in public materials.

The product portfolio centers on surgical devices designed to simplify procedures and reduce reliance on manual assistance. Flagship products include the Galaxy II self-retaining surgical retractor, the HandMe retractor for hand surgery, the LUX Connect flexible surgical light, Oxiplex adhesion barriers for intrauterine or peritoneal surgery, and the Thermablate EAS portable balloon system for heavy menstrual bleeding. The group sells in more than 40 countries through local distribution partners; facility size, headcount, and production volumes are not publicly specified.

Primary customers are healthcare providers, including the U.K. National Health Service (NHS) and private hospital groups such as Circle Health Group, Nuffield Health, and Ramsay Healthcare. The Swedish subsidiary, JUNE Medical Sverige AB, handles direct sales to Swedish healthcare and serves as the EU Authorized Representative for the group. Mosaic Surgical additionally offers U.K. Responsible Person services for other manufacturers seeking to place medical devices on the U.K. market.

The company states its purpose as improving access to medical devices, building partnerships for safer surgery, and reducing the environmental impact of surgery. Differentiators highlighted include the HandMe retractor eliminating the need for an extra pair of hands during operations, the Galaxy II retractor lowering cost and environmental footprint while replacing an assistant, and the LUX Connect light offering unlimited positioning flexibility. The quality policy, authorized by CEO Angela Spang, emphasizes customer focus, continual improvement, and evidence-based decision making.', certifications=ARRAY[]::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Self-Retaining Surgical Retractor", "Adhesion Barriers", "Colposcopy", "Bulking Agent", "UK Responsible Person Services", "Medical Education", "Early-stage innovation", "Research and development", "Manufacturing management", "Global commercialization", "EU Authorized Representative services", "UK Authorized Representative services"], "industries": ["Healthcare", "Medical Devices", "Surgical Instruments", "National Health Service (NHS)", "Private Healthcare Providers", "Women''s Health", "Gynecology", "Obstetrics", "Colorectal Surgery", "Hand Surgery"], "materials": [], "equipment": [], "volume": "", "lead_time": "", "tolerances": "", "built_on": ["Self-retaining retractor replaces surgical assistant", "Lightweight, portable balloon system for heavy menstrual bleeding", "Surgical light with flexible, endless positioning", "Adhesion barriers with decades of safety and efficacy evidence", "UK Responsible Person services for medical device manufacturers"], "facts_used": ["HQ in New Castle, Delaware -> db", "Privately owned medical device group with offices in UK, USA, Sweden -> db", "Sister company Mosaic Surgical acts as manufacturing arm -> db", "Product portfolio includes Galaxy II, HandMe, LUX Connect, Oxiplex, Thermablate -> db", "Sells in over 40 countries through local partners -> db", "Name JUNE originated as secret code n