UPDATE companies SET description='Jones Plastic & Engineering was founded in 1961 in Louisville, Kentucky, by Harry and Larry Jones as a single-machine operation producing whiskey bottle caps. The family-owned business, now headed by the second and third generations of the Jones family, is based in Jeffersontown, Kentucky, and operates nine facilities across the United States and Mexico.

The company provides integrated plastic manufacturing services, including product development, tooling, injection molding (65 to 3,150 tons across five facilities), robotic paint, hydrographics, assembly, and testing. A dedicated 90,000-square-foot paint and hydrographics plant in Juárez, Mexico, houses a 25,000-square-foot clean-room paint line with FANUC robots, RFID-controlled rack systems, and a 1.3-meter hydrographic dip tank. An in-house 3D printing lab runs FDM and PolyJet systems for functional prototypes and short-run injection molded samples. Total manufacturing space approaches 1.6 million square feet with roughly 3,000 employees.

Jones Plastic serves automotive, appliance, powersports, outdoor products, consumer goods, and industrial and defense markets, supplying components and assemblies to North American OEMs. The company also operates Rev-A-Shelf, a wholly owned subsidiary that manufactures residential cabinet storage and organizational products.

The firm pioneered gas-assist injection molding in the early 1990s and emphasizes an engineering-first approach, using solid modeling, CAE simulation, and rapid prototyping to validate designs before tooling. Integrating molding, finishing, and assembly under one supply chain aims to reduce freight, handling, and coordination costs. Quality management is ISO 9001 certified.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Injection molding (65\u20133,150 tons)", "Gas-assist injection molding (GAIM)", "Insert molding", "Overmolding", "In-mold labeling", "Robotic assembly", "Robotic paint", "Hydrographics", "Pad printing", "Hot stamping", "Heat transfer labeling", "Laser etching", "Assembly and testing (pressure decay leak testing, destructive testing, dimensional checks)", "Prototyping (FDM, PolyJet, 3D-printed molds for short-run injection molding)", "Tooling management (mold design, construction, PPAP, mold maintenance, engineering changes)", "Product development (solid modeling, industrial design, photorealistic rendering, CAE simulation, FEA)", "Material selection guidance", "Value-added services (material selection, insert molding, overmolding, gas-assist, robotic assembly, in-mold labeling)", "Decoration (in-mold labeling, hot stamping, pad printing, heat transfer labeling, laser etching)", "Painting and hydrographics (clean-room paint line, FANUC robots, RFID-controlled rack systems, hydrographic dip)", "Warehousing and logistics"], "industries": ["Automotive", "Appliance", "Powersports", "Outdoor products", "Consumer goods", "Industrial and defense"], "materials": ["Commodity thermoplastics", "Engineering-grade thermoplastics"], "equipment": ["FANUC robots", "RFID-controlled rack systems", "1.3-meter hydrographic dip tank", "FDM 3D printers", "PolyJet 3D printers", "PTC Creo (CAD software)", "Moldex3D (mold filling analysis software)", "Finite element analysis (FEA) software", "Stack molds", "MUD base molds"], "volume": "", "lead_time":