UPDATE companies SET description='K & F Electronics was founded in 1972 in Fraser, Michigan, a suburb of Detroit. The company began as a single facility focused on integrated circuit board solutions.

Today, K & F operates from its Fraser facility with a team of 27 professionals. It provides end-to-end PCB services: in-house fabrication of single-sided, double-sided, and multilayer rigid boards (up to IPC Class 3), as well as flex and rigid-flex circuits using materials such as FR-4, Rogers, Taconic, Arlon, Nelco, Teflon, polyimide, and aluminum. Assembly capabilities include automated SMT (18,000–30,000 components per hour), through-hole, selective soldering, box build, and hand soldering. The company also offers PCB design, reverse engineering, 3D printing, wire stripping, conformal coating, flying probe testing, and X-ray/AOI inspection. Offshore partnerships supplement high-volume production.

Customers range from prototype runs to high-volume orders, with expedited lead times from 24 hours to four weeks.

K & F differentiates itself through an integrated design-fabrication-assembly model, a 1-year warranty on all PCBs and PCBAs, and a reported return rate below 1%. Its motto, “Providing quality today for tomorrow’s technology,” reflects a legacy of reliability and a commitment to domestic PCB production as a PCBAA member.', certifications=ARRAY['ISO 9001:2015','ITAR','RoHS','UL Approved #E71379','IPC-6012 Class 1-3']::text[], profile='{"capabilities": ["Single-sided PCB fabrication", "Double-sided PCB fabrication", "Multilayer PCB fabrication (up to IPC Class 3)", "Buried/blind via PCB fabrication", "Flex circuit fabrication", "Rigid-flex PCB fabrication", "Rogers/Taconic/Arlon/Nelco laminate processing", "Aluminum PCB fabrication", "Surface mount technology (SMT) assembly", "Through-hole (THT) assembly", "Box build assembly", "Hand soldering", "Selective soldering", "Automated optical inspection (AOI) 2D/3D", "X-ray inspection", "Flying probe electrical testing", "Conformal coating (acrylic)", "PCB drilling and routing", "PCB design and layout engineering", "Schematic design", "Bill of materials (BOM) generation", "Reverse engineering and scanning", "3D printing for prototypes", "Wire stripping", "Expedited manufacturing (24-hour to 4-week)"], "industries": ["Electronics manufacturing", "Aerospace and defense", "Medical devices", "Industrial electronics"], "materials": ["FR-4", "Rogers RO4350B", "Taconic", "Arlon", "Nelco", "Teflon (PTFE)", "Polyimide", "Aluminum", "Flex circuit substrates", "Acrylic conformal coating"], "equipment": ["VJ Electronix XQuik II X-Ray parts counter", "Fancort Industries VPD3-1S scoring/depaneling machine"], "volume": "Prototype to high-volume production (SMT capacity 18,000\u201330,000 components/hour)", "lead_time": "Expedited options from 24 hours to 4 weeks; same-day assembly start after component receipt", "tolerances": "Board dimensional tolerances up to IPC Class 3; conformal coating thickness \u00b15 \u00b5m (non-electro) and \u0